Subject: [PATCH] fix(asks): the person the owner named is first even when the
 title leaves them out (1691)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 49996, 0 of 1: the owner wrote „…პირველ რიგში ციცინო
ფილტრაძეს ჰკითხე, მერე სხვებსაც.". The plan text put her first. The ranking
had her named_by_goal false, and she ranked last. The wave order looked
for named people only in the goal's title. The title is the model's wording
of the goal, and it left her out.

The order now looks for them in the title AND in the owner's own lines in
the goal's conversation: from just before the goal opened, newest 20, each
cut at 500 characters. The waves (readWave) and the admin read use the same
text. A failed read ranks by the title alone, as before. The pre-match
words and the answer-stats field still come from the title, so the records
are read where the asks file them.

Also from 49996: GET /admin/goals/:id/wave-ranking reads a proposed plan
(the proposal waiting on the owner wins when both exist), and says which,
in plan_state. The order can now be judged before anything is sent.

DONE WHEN: „პირველ რიგში X-ს ჰკითხე" puts X first in the ranking
(named_by_goal true), and the rest keep their record order; the read works
on the plan card, before approval.

